course: dictionary
lesson: 3973
title: Names with capital letters: Gabriel
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A proper noun is the name of one particular person, place or thing, and it always starts with a capital letter. Gabriel is a proper noun. The clues around it tell you which Gabriel is meant.
explain: «The angel Gabriel told Mary in Nazareth that she would have a son.» The word angel and the story of Mary are clues. Here Gabriel is a messenger in a religious story, not a boy in your class.
explain: «Fahrenheit is named after Daniel Gabriel Fahrenheit, a German-speaking scientist.» Here Gabriel sits in the middle of a person's full name, so it is a man's name. The capital letter shows it is a name, not just a word.
fact: A proper noun is a special name, and it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Gabriel can be the name of an angel, a messenger of God in Christianity.
fact: In Islam, Muslims believe the angel Jibril (Gabriel) brought the words of the Qur'an to the Prophet Muhammad.
fact: Gabriel is also a boy's or man's name.
fact: The Annunciation is the story of the angel Gabriel telling Mary that she would have a son, Jesus.
exercise: «The angel Gabriel told Mary in Nazareth that she would have a son.» Who is Gabriel in this sentence? | A teacher at school | *A messenger angel | A town far away | A type of bird
exercise: In «Daniel Gabriel Fahrenheit, a German-speaking scientist», what is Gabriel? | *A middle name, a man's name | A kind of angel | A type of food | A city in Germany
exercise: Why does Gabriel start with a capital letter? | *It is a proper noun, the name of one particular person or angel | Every noun starts with a capital letter | It is at the start of a sentence every time | It is a long word
test: In the Bible, what does the angel Gabriel tell Mary? | She will move to a new town | *She will have a son, Jesus | She will become a queen | She will win a race
test: Which word is a proper noun? | told | *Gabriel | messenger | angel
exam: Muslims believe Gabriel (Jibril) brought what to the Prophet Muhammad? | A map of the world | A new song | A letter from the king | *The words of the Qur'an
